[{:db/id 17592186059687 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cf7bb594-de49-54f5-b420-2e5186a68020" "question-4ffccd8c-fd28-5be4-b193-a3d833fff80a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cf7bb594-de49-54f5-b420-2e5186a68020" :question/id #uuid "cf7bb594-de49-54f5-b420-2e5186a68020" :question/math-academy-id "q-182569" :question/problem "$\\,$ If you don't turn the volume up, then you won't hear what they're saying.\n\nWhich statement is logically equivalent to the conditional statement above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ You don't turn the volume up.\n\n- $B:$ You won't hear what they're saying.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A⇒B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬A∨B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You turn the volume up.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ You turn the volume up, or you won't hear what they're saying.\n\nWe can write this in more everyday language as follows:\n\n$\\,$ Turn the volume up, or you won't hear what they're saying." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d4b159f-3c60-5c4b-a838-942cc712f24e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d4b159f-3c60-5c4b-a838-942cc712f24e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4b159f-3c60-5c4b-a838-942cc712f24e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a936808b-8124-518b-b459-f435422af3d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc2fdd88-5b07-5cc9-9f2d-69efb801b26a" "answer-8529207d-33ec-5310-8f93-ac4dc4020cb5" "answer-ca1701d1-8ce6-5bed-8a35-b8cf1174656f" "answer-309deb5e-b30d-502d-b896-e1f163bb596b" "answer-a936808b-8124-518b-b459-f435422af3d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc2fdd88-5b07-5cc9-9f2d-69efb801b26a" :answer/id #uuid "dc2fdd88-5b07-5cc9-9f2d-69efb801b26a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :