zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6243668f-f17a-5b03-913e-72b8f476068f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6243668f-f17a-5b03-913e-72b8f476068f" :answer-field/id #uuid "6243668f-f17a-5b03-913e-72b8f476068f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2513616-2a1d-50a1-8859-18c121631f3a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a11ca8b-4db9-5745-913c-b7d2c822948d" "answer-fabc6d0a-ca89-586c-90d6-3e44b1de752e" "answer-62f6689c-e1aa-59c6-969a-a053017be4a7" "answer-a2513616-2a1d-50a1-8859-18c121631f3a" "answer-6fa409c9-3b6c-521c-8018-31c3aa75ce9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a11ca8b-4db9-5745-913c-b7d2c822948d" :answer/id #uuid "1a11ca8b-4db9-5745-913c-b7d2c822948d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Don't submit your assignment, and you won't get a zero." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fabc6d0a-ca89-586c-90d6-3e44b1de752e" :answer/id #uuid "fabc6d0a-ca89-586c-90d6-3e44b1de752e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Either you do not submit your assignment, or you will get a zero." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62f6689c-e1aa-59c6-969a-a053017be4a7" :answer/id #uuid "62f6689c-e1aa-59c6-969a-a053017be4a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Either you do not submit your assignment, or you won't get a zero." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2513616-2a1d-50a1-8859-18c121631f3a" :answer/id #uuid "a2513616-2a1d-50a1-8859-18c121631f3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Submit your assignment, or you will get a zero." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fa409c9-3b6c-521c-8018-31c3aa75ce9b" :answer/id #uuid "6fa409c9-3b6c-521c-8018-31c3aa75ce9b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Submit your assignment, or you won't get a zero." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060421 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d17f8721-9970-54a5-a0a5-023397a542c4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d17f8721-9970-54a5-a0a5-023397a542c4" :question/id #uuid "d17f8721-9970-54a5-a0a5-023397a542c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-102734" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(¬A∨¬B)⇒¬A.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∨¬B)⇒¬A≡¬(¬(¬A∨¬B))∨¬A.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(¬A∨¬B))∨¬A≡(¬A∨¬B)∨¬A.\n$$\n\nUsing the commutative and associative law, we have\n\n$$\n(¬A∨¬B)∨¬A≡(¬A∨¬A)∨¬B.\n$$\n\nFinally, by the idempotent law, we have\n\n$$\n(¬A∨¬A)∨¬B≡¬A∨¬B.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬A∨¬B.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd4d4d26-9774-5101-8a1e-2da3a880ab36"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd4d4d26-9774-5101-8a1e-2da3a880ab36" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd4d4d26-9774-5101-8a1e-2da3a880ab36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-deb962e3-f3bf-5667-9728-d3ff4fdfa513" :answer-field/choices ["answer-425436d7-4f12-57df-915c-487746dbd6ca" "answer-c11456cc-728e-58e8-949d-a75492351b19" "answer-751c4258-966c-5529-941d-de9c9266930c" "answer-785c00c3-47f5-5e21-bd85-d44b5a2ca5ff" "answer-deb962e3-f3bf-5667-9728-d3ff4fdfa513"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-425436d7-4f12-57df-915c-487746dbd6ca" :answer/id #uuid "425436d7-4f12-57df-915c-487746dbd6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∨B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c11456cc-728e-58e8-949d-a75492351b19" :answer/id #uuid "c11456cc-728e-58e8-949d-a75492351b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-751c4258-966c-5529-941d-de9c9266930c" :answer/id #uuid "751c4258-966c-5529-941d-de9c9266930c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬A∧¬B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-785c00c3-47f5-5e21-bd85-d44b5a2ca5ff" :answer/id #uuid "785c00c3-47f5-5e21-bd85-d44b5a2ca5ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬A∨B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-deb962e3-f3bf-5667-9728-d3ff4fdfa513" :answer/id #uuid "deb962e3-f3bf-5667-9728-d3ff4fdfa513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬A∨¬B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a315de4-d76f-5902-ac75-57586afb2f01"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a315de4-d76f-5902-ac75-57586afb2f01" :question/id #uuid "5a315de4-d76f-5902-ac75-57586afb2f01" :question/math-academy-id "q-316642" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad5ee5c0c388e0d2a800765288f20350a8332888a54b4eb3fafd5986d6355838.png)\n\nThe line shown above passes through the points $(0,3)$ and $(-2,-1).$ What is the equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,3).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=3.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,3)$ and $(-2,-1),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-3}{-2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=2$ and the $y$-intercept $b=3$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=2x+3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd5cb081-453f-5660-95d6-9625673b4cec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd5cb081-453f-5660-95d6-9625673b4cec" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5cb081-453f-5660-95d6-9625673b4cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa6cfee1-f4ba-5337-94cd-fc676ebd72db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92631607-7e58-5fa5-96af-a13cddef33d4" "answer-aa6cfee1-f4ba-5337-94cd-fc676ebd72db" "answer-b049026b-520e-5374-ad90-addb17c92919" "answer-caba64b7-7134-5366-a184-b1d536fbbf43" "answer-600192ae-60ff-5dcf-8c7b-46a96bdfa607"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92631607-7e58-5fa5-96af-a13cddef33d4" :answer/id #uuid "92631607-7e58-5fa5-96af-a13cddef33d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa6cfee1-f4ba-5337-94cd-fc676ebd72db" :answer/id #uuid "aa6cfee1-f4ba-5337-94cd-fc676ebd72db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b049026b-520e-5374-ad90-addb17c92919" :answer/id #uuid "b049026b-520e-5374-ad90-addb17c92919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caba64b7-7134-5366-a184-b1d536fbbf43" :answer/id #uuid "caba64b7-7134-5366-a184-b1d536fbbf43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-600192ae-60ff-5dcf-8c7b-46a96bdfa607" :answer/id #uuid "600192ae-60ff-5dcf-8c7b-46a96bdfa607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bf74267c-d6a7-5491-a319-f2e29a265fc9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf74267c-d6a7-5491-a319-f2e29a265fc9" :question/id #uuid "bf74267c-d6a7-5491-a319-f2e29a265fc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-215492" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|12z+7|\\ge 5.$\n\n$z\\le$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$ or $\\,z$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $12z+7$ whose distance from zero is greater than or equal to $5.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12z+7 & \\le -5 & \\text{or} &  & 12z+7 & \\ge 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12z+7 & \\le -5 &  &  & 12z+7 & \\ge 5 \\\\ 12z & \\le -12 &  &  & 12z & \\ge -2 \\\\ z & \\le -1 &  &  & z & \\ge -\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & \\le -1 & \\text{or} &  & z & \\ge -\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bf84b07b-a308-558a-9ef5-8ba63478514c" "answer-field-07839e3e-5717-5971-8c55-29675d677717" "answer-field-ea10f362-1845-5a00-a8ef-b90f7c8afd1f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf84b07b-a308-558a-9ef5-8ba63478514c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf84b07b-a308-558a-9ef5-8ba63478514c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ce6d3593-b9ee-56e6-a313-b289f3e83396" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce6d3593-b9ee-56e6-a313-b289f3e83396"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce6d3593-b9ee-56e6-a313-b289f3e83396" :answer/id #uuid "ce6d3593-b9ee-56e6-a313-b289f3e83396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07839e3e-5717-5971-8c55-29675d677717" :answer-field/id #uuid "07839e3e-5717-5971-8c55-29675d677717" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1fea0b29-7f79-50a0-a2d0-ce5d93803b92" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1fea0b29-7f79-50a0-a2d0-ce5d93803b92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fea0b29-7f79-50a0-a2d0-ce5d93803b92" :answer/id #uuid "1fea0b29-7f79-50a0-a2d0-ce5d93803b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea10f362-1845-5a00-a8ef-b90f7c8afd1f" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea10f362-1845-5a00-a8ef-b90f7c8afd1f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5fc9f90b-a8c3-59ba-9cd9-45a1d4218177" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5fc9f90b-a8c3-59ba-9cd9-45a1d4218177"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fc9f90b-a8c3-59ba-9cd9-45a1d4218177" :answer/id #uuid "5fc9f90b-a8c3-59ba-9cd9-45a1d4218177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096654 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-06291cf0-d6c5-5a7a-a5c7-3922a0916c3b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-06291cf0-d6c5-5a7a-a5c7-3922a0916c3b" :question/id #uuid "06291cf0-d6c5-5a7a-a5c7-3922a0916c3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11749" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e0caa2bd7ac6b620ec267d3cc50493701af1f2d6718ddcb090c71f408d2a82ab.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{b}$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following could be $-b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We interpret  $-b+c$ as the addition\n\n$$\n(-b)+c,\n$$\n\nwhere $-b$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $b$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $b.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $-b$ and $c:$ \n\n- We can start $-b$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $c$ and has its tail placed at the head of $-b.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $-\\text{b}$ to the head of $\\text{c}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/87/873334db27c4cf2d85d262d98050941307026fb7b0341d5c871a5ad8eb565313.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79a697f6-597e-5bb5-9a8f-fc97fd26f368"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79a697f6-597e-5bb5-9a8f-fc97fd26f368" :answer-field/id #uuid "79a697f6-597e-5bb5-9a8f-fc97fd26f368" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-611a8a2b-1562-5fd6-98e4-b824b2c679fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8912cd22-1c74-5633-8023-b8ecb0a0fad5" "answer-4dc35e4c-9a9c-5ceb-a076-e19bcff1531f" "answer-611a8a2b-1562-5fd6-98e4-b824b2c679fc" "answer-e27d143e-c634-541c-b918-53132ea5460b" "answer-39706a6d-e9a6-5650-b5b2-4d251ac0aa89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8912cd22-1c74-5633-8023-b8ecb0a0fad5" :answer/id #uuid "8912cd22-1c74-5633-8023-b8ecb0a0fad5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/24/24956401d3bd15e50cd6396fdd6eb99c267d7d810965631c85cdb9b34d525a89.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dc35e4c-9a9c-5ceb-a076-e19bcff1531f" :answer/id #uuid "4dc35e4c-9a9c-5ceb-a076-e19bcff1531f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/86/867d2f76ab683e7c5ae703f99e2a229e8fbbc0951f3d75ef880a6cea3e110f21.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-611a8a2b-1562-5fd6-98e4-b824b2c679fc" :answer/id #uuid "611a8a2b-1562-5fd6-98e4-b824b2c679fc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a7/a7f080d33b393ffe9742aa14bc05116a5dec270802529e3d0d57133914a5390c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e27d143e-c634-541c-b918-53132ea5460b" :answer/id #uuid "e27d143e-c634-541c-b918-53132ea5460b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/bf/bf733d5afc13934a4d75a0fce57a0b6f96ffd9d5032200bb105adb2cc87d73dc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39706a6d-e9a6-5650-b5b2-4d251ac0aa89" :answer/id #uuid "39706a6d-e9a6-5650-b5b2-4d251ac0aa89" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d4/d4a39433da61674389a83f6d43b44f0ecbf129cf264879b863934f383897d9ab.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064239 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46ac0cd5-cca2-5b10-8e71-7bc6828cb573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-46ac0cd5-cca2-5b10-8e71-7bc6828cb573" :question/id #uuid "46ac0cd5-cca2-5b10-8e71-7bc6828cb573" :question/math-academy-id "q-156126" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}p-2>3 \\\\ 1-2p\\le -7\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $p$ that satisfy both $p-2>3$ and $1-2p\\le -7$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $p-2>3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p-2 & >3 \\\\ p-2+2 & >3+2 \\\\ p & >5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/11/1189f49b694afcfef7f10a19b523ebbcce3bb8ab13b69e60ebfd5a6c342ff10e.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $1-2p\\le -7\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2p & \\le -7 \\\\ 1-2p-1 & \\le -7-1 \\\\ -2p & \\le -8 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2p) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ 2p & \\ge 8 \\\\ \\frac{2p}{2} & \\ge \\frac{8}{2} \\\\ p & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f8/f8bf3ae94c8048dcf9060c985300f9a808ae73158eeeef6e0f01f3f922d33ea9.png)\n\nTo find the values of $p$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/1a/1a4cd0c86983a39354eef09ad60d44f3815c082f443a3eb12bd14f6232988f65.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $p\\in (5,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4b7ff8f-af4b-55e7-a7df-45025547835b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4b7ff8f-af4b-55e7-a7df-45025547835b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4b7ff8f-af4b-55e7-a7df-45025547835b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e3c70cb9-1512-5f74-8095-ae65fd580c38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a48122cf-62c6-51b8-baec-3d0e7d115657" "answer-6d46c113-ad6c-5e71-975b-24d9fa413748" "answer-4e674786-3773-5608-a6fc-fb98f442c244" "answer-e3c70cb9-1512-5f74-8095-ae65fd580c38" "answer-bc69fc81-dde3-504b-9bdc-e9632904c364"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a48122cf-62c6-51b8-baec-3d0e7d115657" :answer/id #uuid "a48122cf-62c6-5