tep "step-9715ff39-e143-57b2-b4c6-3548f3a39516" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-9715ff39-e143-57b2-b4c6-3548f3a39516" :step/id #uuid "9715ff39-e143-57b2-b4c6-3548f3a39516" :step/content 17592186129760 :step/next "step-0a8e6389-a5e8-5f3f-9c7c-f7d9c66a8d2a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0a8e6389-a5e8-5f3f-9c7c-f7d9c66a8d2a" :step/id #uuid "0a8e6389-a5e8-5f3f-9c7c-f7d9c66a8d2a" :step/content 17592186482583 :step/next "step-382931c6-b743-51fa-94c1-914653e20d3a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-382931c6-b743-51fa-94c1-914653e20d3a" :step/id #uuid "382931c6-b743-51fa-94c1-914653e20d3a" :step/content 17592186482576 :step/next "step-54e611fd-f6c1-51a3-942a-952198e2cfcd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-54e611fd-f6c1-51a3-942a-952198e2cfcd" :step/id #uuid "54e611fd-f6c1-51a3-942a-952198e2cfcd" :step/content 17592186374048 :step/next "step-abbf1f47-5dfa-5835-9d87-a03c6c72b6c2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-abbf1f47-5dfa-5835-9d87-a03c6c72b6c2" :step/id #uuid "abbf1f47-5dfa-5835-9d87-a03c6c72b6c2" :step/content 17592186374055 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060316 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059654 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5021d5eb-c519-52ae-b30c-1049345fdc26"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5021d5eb-c519-52ae-b30c-1049345fdc26" :question/id #uuid "5021d5eb-c519-52ae-b30c-1049345fdc26" :question/math-academy-id "q-6423" :question/problem "A triangle has sides $m$, $n$, and $o.$ The sides $m$, $n$, and $o$ are of lengths  $2$, $5$, and $6$, respectively. What is the measure of the angle between the sides $n$ and $o?$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](images/26/26f2041aec84bb0086e2f08c2ba3a19331895951782b7fda153858643a8a5dd4.png)\n\nWe use the Law of Cosines to solve for angle $M:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡M & =\\frac{{o}^{2}+{n}^{2}-{m}^{2}}{2no}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm=2,\\,n=5,\\,o=6.\n$$\n\nThis gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡M & =\\frac{{6}^{2}+{5}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{2(5)(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{36+25-4}{60} \\\\  & =\\frac{57}{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠M & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{57}{60}) \\\\  & ={18.19}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe46b4b1-2f2f-5fb3-9e1d-afbfc19fa446"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe46b4b1-2f2f-5fb3-9e1d-afbfc19fa446" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe46b4b1-2f2f-5fb3-9e1d-afbfc19fa446" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c646cdc4-684d-54a1-8714-3eeef1e84d61" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9b37447-949a-5c58-9208-515eaa569613" "answer-6437eb0c-5020-559e-bd70-319aee5ba937" "answer-c646cdc4-684d-54a1-8714-3eeef1e84d61" "answer-d4bc5f15-b8d5-57ea-919a-885ac1bd4741" "answer-1f7d18b7-8669-51a0-8612-923a2719727c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9b37447-949a-5c58-9208-515eaa569613" :answer/id #uuid "c9b37447-949a-5c58-9208-515eaa569613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{16.43}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6437eb0c-5020-559e-bd70-319aee5ba937" :answer/id #uuid "6437eb0c-5020-559e-bd70-319aee5ba937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{17.89}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c646cdc4-684d-54a1-8714-3eeef1e84d61" :answer/id #uuid "c646cdc4-684d-54a1-8714-3eeef1e84d61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{18.19}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4bc5f15-b8d5-57ea-919a-885ac1bd4741" :answer/id #uuid "d4bc5f15-b8d5-57ea-919a-885ac1bd4741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{20.36}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f7d18b7-8669-51a0-8612-923a2719727c" :answer/id #uuid "1f7d18b7-8669-51a0-8612-923a2719727c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{21.20}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059653 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-edd7453d-0827-54b9-87f7-014fa66cf7ec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-edd7453d-0827-54b9-87f7-014fa66cf7ec" :question/id #uuid "edd7453d-0827-54b9-87f7-014fa66cf7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-14506" :question/problem "A triangle has sides $j$, $k$, and $l.$ The sides $j$ and $l$ have lengths $4$ and $7$, respectively. If the angle $K$ between $j$ and $l$ has a measure of ${121}^{∘}$, what is the length of side $k?$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](images/1f/1fde3029f6a50388ebd342dc4d15e9787567461b651c24cd6bd6843521b0465d.png)\n\nThe Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\n{k}^{2}={j}^{2}+{l}^{2}-2jl\\operatorname{cos}⁡K.\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm∠K={121}^{∘},\\,j=4,\\,l=7.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{7}^{2}-2(4)(7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{121}^{∘} \\\\  & =16+49-56\\operatorname{cos}⁡{121}^{∘} \\\\  & =65-56(-0.515\\,03…) \\\\  & =65+28.842\\,13 \\\\  & =93.842\\,13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\nk=\\sqrt{93.842\\,13}=9.69\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e61d7995-875b-5a12-bc2c-d4a1dc9575fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e61d7995-875b-5a12-bc2c-d4a1dc9575fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "e61d7995-875b-5a12-bc2c-d4a1dc9575fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f46016ce-d644-5ff1-b8c1-c24047295c26" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e6bcf4ed-a6f1-5dad-93c0-7edac4fd7cfe" "answer-8be15e53-3455-5a