pe :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0095370a-c8b2-539f-b84a-3358daac6e06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0095370a-c8b2-539f-b84a-3358daac6e06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0095370a-c8b2-539f-b84a-3358daac6e06" :answer/id #uuid "0095370a-c8b2-539f-b84a-3358daac6e06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da16c186-641b-5260-a847-c6013431f279" :answer-field/id #uuid "da16c186-641b-5260-a847-c6013431f279" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-21b6f4c8-9c0c-5da8-a676-422820235afd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21b6f4c8-9c0c-5da8-a676-422820235afd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21b6f4c8-9c0c-5da8-a676-422820235afd" :answer/id #uuid "21b6f4c8-9c0c-5da8-a676-422820235afd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060041 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-d424dcb1-177c-5053-898f-bbc5de5cd766" :question/id #uuid "d424dcb1-177c-5053-898f-bbc5de5cd766" :question/math-academy-id "q-125100" :question/problem "If $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨4,-3⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨-1,2⟩$, then $2\\overset{\\to }{u}+\\overset{\\to }{v}=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{\\to }{u}+\\overset{\\to }{v} & =2\\cdot ⟨4,-3⟩+⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-6⟩+⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8+(-1),-6+2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8-1,-6+2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbdfce8f-abfe-53cb-9705-5a4369c47f42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbdfce8f-abfe-53cb-9705-5a4369c47f42" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbdfce8f-abfe-53cb-9705-5a4369c47f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b3488a28-3a50-53c3-80e7-a44957ccecfe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-564f131c-8153-5250-b192-4b9c01928dac" "answer-6a83b317-aff4-5937-af17-51947b81c9ad" "answer-e7674bcd-8b37-50a7-9442-93d15edfb14d" "answer-b3488a28-3a50-53c3-80e7-a44957ccecfe" "answer-9583fb5a-80a8-59d4-8f69-e42a4c690518"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-564f131c-8153-5250-b192-4b9c01928dac" :answer/id #uuid "564f131c-8153-5250-b192-4b9c01928dac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-7,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a83b317-aff4-5937-af17-51947b81c9ad" :answer/id #uuid "6a83b317-aff4-5937-af17-51947b81c9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7674bcd-8b37-50a7-9442-93d15edfb14d" :answer/id #uuid "e7674bcd-8b37-50a7-9442-93d15edfb14d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,-6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3488a28-3a50-53c3-80e7-a44957ccecfe" :answer/id #uuid "b3488a28-3a50-53c3-80e7-a44957ccecfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨7,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9583fb5a-80a8-59d4-8f69-e42a4c690518" :answer/id #uuid "9583fb5a-80a8-59d4-8f69-e42a4c690518" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨9,-6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060907 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given two vectors \n$\\mathbf{a} = \\langle 2,3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\langle -4,4 \\rangle,$ shown below. How do we compute the vectors $\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}$  and  $-5\\mathbf{a}$ in terms of the standard basis $\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j}?$\n\n![](images/25/254809cbc834b493759a6fa09222a2c90c5fbfc3280d22e82470e760a7a4c508.png)\n\nTo compute $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b},$ we collect all of the $\\mathbf{i}$'s and $\\mathbf{j}$'s. We know that $\\mathbf{a} = {\\color{red}2}\\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}3}\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = {\\color{red}-4}\\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}4}\\mathbf{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =(2i+3j)+(-4i+4j) \\\\  & =(2+(-4))i+(3+4)j \\\\  & =-2i+7j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n![](images/ea/eae25a74dde73f7899f6ccbbdbb1a1f589fc72cad9629a33b4fdbbbc753efcd8.svg)\n\nTo compute $-5\\mathbf{a},$ we multiply each of the components by $-5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot a & =-5(2i+3j) \\\\  & =(-5\\cdot 2)i+(-5\\cdot 3)j \\\\  & =-10i+-15j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n![](images/05/05f847a73201db3de20db3847ef4ed97e07ea7fae9325401b1ea5a460968f9da.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060908 :tutorial/content "To add or subtract vectors given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to add or subtract each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2,5⟩+⟨-3,7⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨2+(-3),5+7⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨-1,12⟩ & ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand in column vector notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+(-3) \\\\ 5+7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, to multiply a vector given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to multiply each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot ⟨2,5⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨(-5)\\cdot 2,(-5)\\cdot 5⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨-10,-25⟩ & ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand in column vector notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060909 :tutorial/content "To denote a vector, we have used two notations:\n\n- a single bold lowercase letter, such as $\\mathbf{v},$ or\n\n- two uppercase letters representing the points of the ends of the vector, with an arrow over them, such as $\\overrightarrow{AB}.$\n\nWe will mostly stick to these notations. However, there are many possible notations for vectors. For example, sometimes a vector can be denoted as\n\n$$\n\\vec{v}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{V}, \\quad v, \\quad \\hat{v}.\n$$\n\nThe rightmost notation, $\\hat{v},$ is usually used to represent unit vectors in particular." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059922 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-070008c9-e913-5456-a5af-e255c5aba081" "question-2e637b5f-6f34-5a1c-b2e1-f9ed9e9b050b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-070008c9-e913-5456-a5af-e255c5aba081" :question/id #uuid "070008c9-e913-5456-a5af-e255c5aba081" :question/math-academy-id "q-30824" :question/problem "${log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt{8})=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=64$ and $X=\\sqrt{8}.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ can be presented as a power of $8,$ we set $b=8.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt{8}) & =\\frac{{log}_{8}⁡(\\sqrt{8})}{{log}_{8}⁡(64)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{8}⁡({8}^{1/2})}{{log}_{8}⁡({8}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd14762e-d61e-513a-9786-dfc287bdc4a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd14762e-d61e-513a-9786-dfc287bdc4a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd14762e-d61e-513a-9786-dfc287bdc4a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-38a98641-2e38-578c-b3c5-17bb1f192700" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e7dce6a-3e36-598d-9a5e-9b0c2908e50b" "answer-9d4fd407-f836-5227-93e6-01c0887c14a9" "answer-e1e77c3b-5d54-5798-8bc6-98d8b4b1e688" "answer-38a98641-2e38-578c-b3c5-17bb1f192700" "answer-9b66ccb7-9147-50dc-a184-c4ff564b8209"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e7dce6a-3e36-598d-9a5e-9b0c2908e50b" :answer/id #uuid "5e7dce6a-3e36-598d-9a5e-9b0c2908e50b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4fd407-f836-5227-93e6-01c0887c14a9" :answer/id #uuid "9d4fd407-f836-5227-93e6-01c0887c14a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1e77c3b-5d54-5798-8bc6-98d8b4b1e688" :answer/id #uuid "e1e77c3b-5d54-5798-8bc6-98d8b4b1e688" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38a98641-2e38-578c-b3c5-17bb1f192700" :answer/id #uuid "38a98641-2e38-578c-b3c5-17bb1f192700" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b66ccb7-9147-50dc-a184-c4ff564b8209" :answer/id #uuid "9b66ccb7-9147-50dc-a184-c4ff564b8209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e637b5f-6f34-5a1c-b2e1-f9ed9e9b050b" :question/id #uuid "2e637b5f-6f34-5a1c-b2e1-f9ed9e9b050b" :question/math-academy-id "q-66885" :question/problem "${log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=64$ and $X=\\sqrt[3]{4}.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ can be presented as a power of $4,$ we set $b=4.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{4}) & =\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{4})}{{log}_{4}⁡(64)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{1/3})}{{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b211c988-c894-53a3-abe3-c7c0de871b39"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b211c988-c894-53a3-abe3-c7c0de871b39" :answer-field/id #uuid "b211c988-c894-53a3-abe3-c7c0de871b39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-66a0bcce-653d-592a-b615-921125e4877d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95204e1c-0acb-54ed-a36a-670e3b50729d" "answer-66a0bcce-653d-592a-b615-921125e4877d" "answer-76ba75fb-4bc9-5ff8-9ed9-b66c1d091c5d" "answer-b82f8830-ef82-53f9-94fe-10a3b6669fdf" "answer-b870fa54-4d3f-51b4-81c7-fd2cf9755718"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95204e1c-0acb-54ed-a36a-670e3b50729d" :answer/id #uuid "95204e1c-0acb-54ed-a36a-670e3b50729d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66a0bcce-653d-592a-b615-921125e4877d" :answer/id #uuid "66a0bcce-653d-592a-b615-921125e4877d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76ba75fb-4bc9-5ff8-9ed9-b66c1d091c5d" :answer/id #uuid "76ba75fb-4bc9-5ff8-9ed9-b66c1d091c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b82f8830-ef82-53f9-94fe-10a3b6669fdf" :answer/id #uuid "b82f8830-ef82-53f9-94fe-10a3b6669fdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b870fa54-4d3f-51b4-81c7-fd2cf9755718" :answer/id #uuid "b870fa54-4d3f-51b4-81c7-fd2cf9755718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3542d0d0-8424-5c15-90db-0d0a314cb9c3" :activity/id #uuid "3542d0d0-8424-5c15-90db-0d0a314cb9c3" :activity/title "The Change of Base Formula for Logarithms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048470 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-bd6d4a94-a1a0-5506-a3c7-6666ea986adc" "step-518c1048-98b7-5c05-bbdd-0b9d19b57a71" "step-5a87c232-6596-5aaf-adc7-7ced8ad66d80"] :activity/first-step "step-bd6d4a94-a1a0-5506-a3c7-6666ea986adc" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-bd6d4a94-a1a0-5506-a3c7-6666ea986adc" :step/id #uuid "bd6d4a94-a1a0-5506-a3c7-6666ea986adc" :step/content 17592186234501 :step/next "step-518c1048-98b7-5c05-bbdd-0b9d19b57a71" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-518c1048-98b7-5c05-bbdd-0b9d19b57a71" :step/id #uuid "518c1048-98b7-5c05-bbdd-0b9d19b57a71" :step/content "question-070008c9-e913-5456-a5af-e255c5aba081" :step/next "step-5a87c232-6596-5aaf-adc7-7ced8ad66d80" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5a87c232-6596-5aaf-adc7-7ced8ad66d80" :step/id #uuid "5a87c232-6596-5aaf-adc7-7ced8ad66d80" :step/content "question-2e637b5f-6f34-5a1c-b2e1-f9ed9e9b050b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0dd8f23a-a284-5af7-a370-b6877f8aea89"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0dd8f23a-a284-5af7-a370-b6877f8aea89" :question/id #uuid "0dd8f23a-a284-5af7-a370-b6877f8aea89" :question/math-academy-id "q-73637" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06426327-a841-5962-9ad3-ae8e7d73820a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06426327-a841-5962-9ad3-ae8e7d73820a" :answer-field/id #uuid "06426327-a841-5962-9ad3-ae8e7d73820a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9c64bb76-0eee-5a58-8335-3ca14cce1cc3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-023cc2f5-0dc4-57b8-83da-cab850c0da1f" "answer-294e94d5-45b0-5fea-8eb3-7cbc5ccb9acb" "answer-8a19af7a-70b9-503e-80be-9feeab7ec744" "answer-9c64bb76-0eee-5a58-8335-3ca14cce1cc3" "answer-43f5998d-2db6-5652-b314-092fcba29772"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-023cc2f5-0dc4-57b8-83da-cab850c0da1f" :answer/id #uuid "023cc2f5-0dc4-57b8-83da-cab850c0da1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-294e94d5-45b0-5fea-8eb3-7cbc5ccb9acb" :answer/id #uuid "294e94d5-45b0-5fea-8eb3-7cbc5ccb9acb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a19af7a-70b9-503e-80be-9feeab7ec744" :answer/id #uuid "8a19af7a-70b9-503e-80be-9feeab7ec744" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd and $4$th" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c64bb76-0eee-5a58-8335-3ca14cce1cc3" :answer/id #uuid "9c64bb76-0eee-5a58-8335-3ca14cce1cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43f5998d-2db6-5652-b314-092fcba29772" :answer/id #uuid "43f5998d-2db6-5652-b314-092fcba29772" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6a7e87a4-1f44-5991-b6ac-4821416eb17f" :activity/id #uuid "6a7e87a4-1f44-5991-b6ac-4821416eb17f" :activity/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049723 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-1b52500c-21bc-5f99-a291-e2b84ac9eab2" "step-a40a64e5-a473-5166-a321-aeb74fa92cf3" "step-2fa9c88c-b6e4-5611-a708-8e19640dbe01" "step-9239f6d7-6799-56eb-8b1c-f9961bb1ed31" "step-887149e4-2501-5d36-ab37-f2b093acd38b"] :activity/first-step "step-1b52500c-21bc-5f99-a291-e2b84ac9eab2" :